# ECG Deck Builder Unity Test

A Unity-based deck building prototype focused on UI systems, animation sequencing, and REST API integration.

Built with:
- Unity 6000.3.6f1
- DOTween
- JSONBin.io
- C#

---

# Features

## Main Menu
- New User flow
- UUID generation and persistence using PlayerPrefs
- Continue button enabled only when a UUID exists

---

## Deck Builder Scene
- 15 unique cards created using ScriptableObjects
- Randomized deck shuffle system
- Interactive card draw flow
- DOTween card animations:
  - Lift
  - Flip
  - Focus zoom
  - Move to hand
- Hand limit of 8 cards
- Save Deck / Discard Deck flow
- Discard reshuffles and rebuilds the deck

---

## Deck Viewer Scene
- Fetches saved decks from JSONBin.io
- Displays multiple saved decks in a scrollable UI
- Click cards to focus/enlarge for readability
- Loading state while fetching API data

---

# Architecture

The project follows a separation-of-concerns approach:

| System | Responsibility |
|---|---|
| DeckSystem | Deck creation, shuffle, draw logic |
| HandSystem | Hand management and capacity |
| APIManager | Cloud save/load communication |
| CardView | Card UI rendering |
| DeckBuilderController | Gameplay flow + animation orchestration |
| DeckViewerController | Deck history visualization |

---

# API Structure

Example JSON structure stored in JSONBin:

```json
{
  "user_id": "uuid",
  "decks": [
    ["1","4","7","9","10","2","11","15"],
    ["3","6","8","12","14","5","1","13"]
  ]
}
```

---

# Controls

| Action | Input |
|---|---|
| Draw Card | Click top deck card |
| Continue Animation | Mouse Click |
| Save Deck | Save Button |
| Discard Deck | Discard Button |
| Focus Card | Click card in Deck Viewer |

---

# Project Structure

```plaintext
Assets/
├── Scripts/
│   ├── Controllers/
│   ├── Systems/
│   ├── API/
│   ├── UI/
│   └── Data/
├── Prefabs/
├── Scenes/
└── ScriptableObjects/
```

---

# Notes

- This project focuses on the deck-building metagame loop only.
- Combat/gameplay systems were intentionally not implemented per assignment scope.
- DOTween is used instead of Animator for procedural UI animation sequencing.

---

# Setup

1. Open project in Unity 6000.3.6f1
2. Import DOTween
3. Add JSONBin URL + API key in `APIManager`
4. Open MainMenu scene
5. Play

